After about six weeks of reading rec.games.hack, and about 5.5 weeks of
dying violently in the Gnomish mines, I've finally gotten a character
who might actually proceed to the Quest.  He's a barbarian, level 11,
and he just finished using up a wand of create monster at the co-aligned
altar in the mine town.

The results, mixed up with the occasional four-leaf clover, were:

	a blessed battle-axe named Cleaver
	an uncursed athame named Magicbane
	an uncursed war hammer named Mjollnir

This is also the order that the weapons appeared in, so I spent some
time wandering around in the Mines with both Cleaver and Magicbane
before Mjollnir appeared (just now).  Magicbane is a useful weapon, to
put it mildly, and I don't have the magic gauntlets I've read about here
that turn Mjollnir into a boomerang, so I'm wondering which of these
weapons would be the best one for me to use.

My Barbarian (named Thundarr, of course; his pet Ookla died on level 2)
doesn't have much else of interest in his inventory:  He's wearing a
ring of teleport control, a +4 elven mithril coat, and carrying the
luckstone from the bottom of the mine.  He is piously neutral, and has
a strength of 17 (18 while wielding Mjollnir).  The only intrinsics I'm
aware of are telepathy, luck, speed, teleport control, random teleport
(ate a leprechaun corpse -- I can't control WHEN I teleport, but I can
decide where to go...) and possibly sleep resistance.

Any tips?

